# Variants are values, not lookup keys

Pass the **variant object** (border, background, badge, …) into viewers.
Do **not** pass a string name and look it up in a shared `VARIANT_CHROME` /
`VARIANT_MAP`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — key + all-styles-knowing map; viewer depends on the map
type VariantName = "default" | "followUp";
const VARIANT_CHROME: Record<VariantName, Chrome> = { … };
viewer: ({ variant }) => <div style={{ color: VARIANT_CHROME[variant].fg }} />
<Item variant="followUp" />

// ✅ GOOD — variant is the chrome itself
type Variant = { fg: string; border: string; background: string; badge: ReactNode };
viewer: ({ variant }) => <div style={{ color: variant.fg }} />
<Item variant={followUpChrome} />
```

## Why

A name-key forces every consumer to share one map that knows every style.
Passing the value keeps chrome host-owned and removes that dependency.

## Phase bags are dicts of values

Hosts still pass a **dictionary keyed by known states** — the entries are
Variant **objects**, not names. Viewers/orchestrators pick by status; they
never consult a second chrome table.

| Phase | Bag shape (per item type) | Pick |
|---|---|---|
| Design | one `Variants` bag (often `{}` / minimal chrome) | use `bag[type]` |
| Responder / review | `Record<ResponderState, Variants>` or dual bags (`variants` / `followUpVariants`) | `bag[status][type]` |

`ResponderState` examples: `default` | `old` | `change` | `error` (host-defined).
`Variant` stays **per type** (`Variants[K]` can differ across `field` / `heading` / …).

```typescript
// ✅ Host builds value bags; resolve picks a value
const fillVariants: Record<"default" | "old" | "change" | "error", Variant> = {
  default: { fg: "#111", border: "#ccc", background: "#fff", badge: null },
  old: { … },
  change: { … },
  error: { … },
};
const variant = fillVariants[status]; // still a Variant object

// ❌ BAD — bag of names + separate chrome map
const names = { default: "default", change: "followUp" };
const chrome = VARIANT_CHROME[names[status]];
```

Storybook controls may still use name keys **at the host boundary** only —
map `TEXT_VARIANT[controlName]` before passing into viewers.

Picking `bag[status]` is not the anti-pattern: the anti-pattern is a
**second** map from name → style that viewers must import.
